      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "HTML::Bare versions through 0.04 for Perl will hang in an infinite loop when parsing malformed attributes.  The parserc_parse function never advances the attribute-parse state cursor on certain malformed attribute forms, looping forever.  Nameless attributes such as \"<a ='c'>\" or unbalanced quotes \"<a b='''''''c'>\" can trigger this condition.  Note that the latest version available on CPAN is version 0.02. Newer versions are available on the git repository.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
